{title: I Have Fought the Good Fight}
{subtitle: Acts 9:1–18; 27:20–44; 2 Timothy 4:6–8}
{key: G#m}
{tempo: 120}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [G#m] | ×16

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
With the high priest's letters and a fire in my veins
I set out for Damascus to bring the Way in chains
Then a light from heaven flashed around me on the road
I fell down to the ground and heard a voice that spoke
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Saul, [F#]Saul, why are you persecuting me
[G#m]Who [F#]are you, Lord
I am Jesus, [D#]whom you are persecuting
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Three days [G#m]I sat in darkness and I would not eat or drink
Till a brother laid his hands on me and pulled me from the brink
Then something like scales fell from my eyes and I could see again
I got up and was baptized and was sent to carry his name
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I have fought the good fight
I have finished the race
I have kept the [F#]faith
I have kept the faith [G#m]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F#]No sun or stars for ma[D#]ny days, the storm kept raging [G#m]on
And all our hope of being saved was finally gone
Then an angel stood beside me and said, Do not be afraid, Paul
The stern broke in the pounding surf, but not one life was lost at all
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I have fought the good fight
I have finished the race
I have kept the faith
I have kept the faith
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
I am [F#]already being poured [F#]out like a drink offering
[D#]The time of my departure [G#m]has come
There is [F#]reserved for me the crown [F#]of righteousness
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I have [D#]fought the good fight
I have fin[G#m]ished the race
I have kept the faith
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
I have kept the faith
{end_of_verse}
